# Oneiron — Memory Wire

> Actor-bound memory for agents. Start with vault.witness, vault.recall and vault.receipts.
> Start with the agent setup guide. The SDK quickstart and error reference below are in this
> repository. The generated reference (types, facade types, verb census) is not published online
> yet; a cargo build keeps a local copy in target/debug/sdk-generated/agent-sdk/.

## Memory Wire SDK

- [Agent setup](docs/agent-setup.md): install from a checkout, start a vault, save and recall over HTTP, connect MCP.
- [Complete quickstarts and API](docs/agent-sdk/quickstart.md): JS/Python, embedded/remote, complete imports and typed errors.
- Type declarations: full TypeScript DTOs and Python stubs, in target/debug/sdk-generated/agent-sdk/types.md after a cargo build.
- Facade types: generated verb wire types, in target/debug/sdk-generated/agent-sdk/facade-types.md after a cargo build.
- [Error catalogue](docs/agent-sdk/errors.md): stable codes, suggestions and remediation.
- Verb census: authoritative shipped facade and stable names, in target/debug/sdk-generated/agent-sdk/verbs.md after a cargo build.
- [Vercel AI SDK tools](packages/oneiron-ai-sdk/README.md): thin three-verb satellite and runnable agent sample.
- [LangGraph BaseStore](packages/oneiron-langgraph/README.md): exact actor-owned long-term keyed memory, not checkpoints.
- [HTTP API](oneiron.skills.md): endpoint activation index, endpoint details and error schemas.
